  "content": {
    "id": "p26-q6-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "Two expressions, $x^{2}+10x+k$ and $x^{2}-10x+k$, are each written in the form $(x+a)^{2}+c$ to give the same value of $c$. Explain why and write down that value of $c$ in terms of $k$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$c=k-25$. Halving the coefficients gives $a=5$ and $a=-5$; both have $a^{2}=25$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^{2}+10x+k&=x^{2}+10x+5^{2}-5^{2}+k\\\\&=(x+5)^{2}+k-25\\\\x^{2}-10x+k&=x^{2}-10x+(-5)^{2}-(-5)^{2}+k\\\\&=(x-5)^{2}+k-25\\end{align*}$$\nIn both cases, $a^{2}=25$, so the same constant is subtracted. Therefore $c=k-25$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 36
  },
